---
// The book's front door: what the book is, and a choice of language.

import { editionHref, editions, site } from '../../book.config.mjs';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
	description="A book about Itinera, a workflow framework that keeps business rules separate from flow control, with an edition for each programming language."
>
	<h1>The Itinera book</h1>
	<p class="lede">
		Itinera is a workflow framework that keeps business rules separate from flow control. This book shows you how to
		build with it, one small online shop at a time.
	</p>
	<p>
		It is one book, written for several programming languages. Pick the language you build with, and read the whole
		book in it: every example is a complete program that compiles and runs, and what it prints is shown underneath.
	</p>
	<p>
		Separating process from logic was good practice before coding agents; now it makes their work safer, because a
		change to a step cannot take a flow decision, and every flow decision is declared in one workflow. <a href={`${site}/why/`}>Why Itinera</a>, on
		the Itinera site, tells that story.
	</p>
	<h2>Pick a language</h2>
	<ul class="edition-list" role="list">
		{
			editions.map((edition) => (
				<li>
					<a href={editionHref(edition)}>
						<span class="edition-list__name">{edition.name}</span>
						<span class="edition-list__detail">
							{edition.released
								? `The whole book, with its examples in ${edition.name}`
								: `The book as it is being written, ahead of the first release, with its examples in ${edition.name}`}
						</span>
					</a>
				</li>
			))
		}
	</ul>
</Base>
